From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:25:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] inputpanel: raise the panel when it is shown
Description:
 The input panel is in the overlay layer, together with layer-shell
 surfaces of the overlay layer. A newly mapped panel is restacked below
 the active window and a panel shown again keeps its position in the
 stacking order. When the focused text input belongs to an overlay
 surface, for example a shell drawer that covers the screen, the panel
 stayed below that surface: it was not visible and touches meant for
 the panel went to that surface.
 .
 Raise the panel whenever it is shown.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
diff --git a/src/inputpanelv1window.cpp b/src/inputpanelv1window.cpp
index 0ac008dd..2041bb16 100644
--- a/src/inputpanelv1window.cpp
+++ b/src/inputpanelv1window.cpp
@@ -250,6 +250,9 @@ void InputPanelV1Window::maybeShow()
         resetPosition();
         markAsMapped();
         setHidden(false);
+        // The panel shares the overlay layer with layer-shell overlay surfaces. Put it on top, otherwise
+        // the panel for a text input in such a surface (e.g. a drawer covering the screen) stays below it.
+        workspace()->raiseWindow(this);
     }
 }
 
